export default "# Vapi | Revenue Recognition Policy\n\n**Policy date:** 2026-03-17\n\nThis policy documents the company's current approach to revenue recognition as an early-stage entity. The company does not yet capture usage consumption data at a level precise enough to support exact drawdown or accrual schedules. The governing principle is that revenue is recognized on the most verifiable basis the company can substantiate — generally cash received or straight-line over the service period. These treatments are interim measures rather than the intended end state and are used because they are what the company's current data can support and substantiate. As usage tracking and reporting mature, recognition will migrate to consumption-based methods for the streams that warrant it. The sections below state each stream's current treatment, the basis for it, and the intended end state.\n\n## Self Serve (Cash Basis Interim, Consumption End)\n\nSelf Serve is a pay-as-you-go B2C channel where customers independently preload their own balances through Stripe. Revenue is recognized on cash received through Stripe, net of Enterprise payments.\n\nThis is a deliberate simplification, and the basis for it differs from the other streams: customers preload balances in advance of use, so cash basis recognizes revenue earlier than a strict transfer-of-control approach would. The company recognizes revenue on cash because Self Serve's usage reporting has been demonstrably unreliable relative to cash collected — recognized revenue exceeded cash collected in 2024, fell below it in 2025, and is showing renewed divergence in 2026 — which means no accrual or consumption-based figure can currently be substantiated. Cash received is the most verifiable basis available for this channel. The company intends to move to a deferred revenue and consumption approach once usage data becomes reliable.\n\n## Enterprise Revenue\n\n### Pilot Periods (Straight-Line)\n\nThe customer pays a non-refundable fee for a defined period of platform access and may elect whether to continue beyond the Pilot. Because continuation is at the customer's election, the enforceable obligation is the Pilot Period itself, and revenue is recognized straight-line over the Pilot duration as access is provided. The defined access period makes this a verifiable basis for recognition.\n\n### Platform License Fees and Recurring Add-ons (Straight-Line)\n\nPlatform License Fees and recurring add-ons (such as HIPAA compliance fees) represent ongoing access to the platform. The customer continuously receives and consumes the benefit of that access as performance occurs, so the obligation is a stand-ready obligation satisfied over time, and a time-based measure of progress best reflects performance. Revenue is recognized straight-line over the applicable service period.\n\n### Usage Minutes & Usage Banks (Straight-Line Interim, Consumption End)\n\nUsage Minutes are prepaid purchases of a defined minute balance consumed over time. Usage Banks are prepaid balances drawn down at contracted variable rates across usage types — compute, text compute, model provider cost passthroughs, and others. The intended treatment for both is consumption-based recognition as the balances are drawn down. Because consumption and usage-type tracking are not yet reliable enough to support accurate drawdown schedules or period-end balance validation, the company defers the prepayment and recognizes it straight-line over the contract term. The amount paid is fully verifiable, and straight-line over the contracted period is the most substantiable systematic measure available until consumption data can support the intended treatment. Recognition will migrate to consumption-based methods once usage reporting supports it.\n\n### Metered Usage (Consumption — Unbilled Receivable)\n\nMetered Usage covers variable consumption rates, minimum commitments, model provider costs, and other variable billing arrangements invoiced in arrears. Revenue is accrued in the period the usage occurs based on the usage data that drives billing, consistent with recognizing revenue as performance occurs. Because these arrangements are billed in arrears, the invoice is itself the substantiation for the amount recognized: usage is measured, billed, and collected after consumption, and recognition follows the billed amount. The underlying usage data may not be precise, but it is the basis on which the company bills for this stream, and the billed amount is therefore the only substantiable figure available for this stream. Because usage is recognized in the period it occurs but invoiced afterward, an unbilled receivable arises at period end for usage delivered but not yet invoiced.\n\nThis distinguishes Metered Usage from the prepaid streams above, where the customer has already paid and the difficulty is releasing that cash through a drawdown schedule the company cannot yet validate. Here the cash has not been received and follows the measured usage that produces the invoice, so recognition rests on the billing event rather than on an estimated release of cash already in hand.\n\n---\n\n## Scope of this agent\n\nThe Vapi RevRec agent handles **Enterprise streams only** (Pilot Periods, Platform License Fees and recurring add-ons, Usage Minutes & Usage Banks, Metered Usage). Self Serve cash-basis recognition is handled by a separate Stripe-ingest workflow and does not flow through this agent. If a contract is identified as Self Serve, the agent should refuse processing and direct the user to the Self Serve workflow.\n\n## Stream-classification quick reference\n\n| Stream | Trigger to classify | Treatment | Interim? | End state |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Pilot Periods | Non-refundable fee, defined Pilot period, customer election to continue | Straight-line over Pilot duration | No | Same |\n| Platform License Fees & Recurring Add-ons | Ongoing platform access fee or recurring add-on (HIPAA, premium support, etc.) | Straight-line over service period | No | Same |\n| Usage Minutes & Usage Banks | **Customer prepays** a balance (minutes or variable-rate bank) to draw down | Straight-line over contract term | **Yes** | Consumption-based drawdown |\n| Metered Usage | Variable billing **invoiced in arrears** after consumption | Consumption in period of usage; unbilled receivable until invoiced | No | Same |\n| Self Serve | B2C, Stripe pay-as-you-go, no MSA | Cash basis | Yes (documented deviation) | Deferred + consumption |\n\nThe single most important distinguishing question for usage-based POs: **does the customer pay UPFRONT for a balance to draw down (Usage Minutes/Banks), or do they pay AFTER consumption based on what they used (Metered Usage)?**\n\nIf the MSA is silent on billing timing, the agent must flag for clarification rather than guess.\n";
